Let’s be honest—fueling up a car is a far cry from stocking a snack bar. If we started offering snacks, it’d be like trying to fit a square peg into a round hole. Imagine our delivery trucks crammed with chips, pretzels, and soda, all while trying to squeeze in a tank of premium unleaded. It’d be like playing Tetris with snacks and gasoline, and we all know how that ends—chaos, crumbs, and spilled fuel!

