Onboarding: Let’s build your page

This form helps us build a fully branded Juiced Fuel location page for your market. The information you provide will be used to create a public-facing page similar to juicedfuel.com/wichita, customized to your city, service area, and ownership team. You do not need to overthink wording or formatting—our team will refine and style everything to match Juiced Fuel brand standards. If you need help in any of the form sections come back and expand the sections below for pointers.

 Contact Information

 

 

 

Provide the best point of contact for onboarding, approvals, and future updates. This information is for internal use and will not automatically be published on your location page unless you include it again in the “Contact the Team” section.

 Location Information

 

 

 

Enter the primary city your franchise serves. This will be used throughout the page for headlines, SEO, and local messaging.
Upload a high-quality photo that visually represents your city (skyline, downtown, waterfront, recognizable streetscape, etc.). Landscape images work best.

 About the City Section

 

 

 

If you would like to write the “About Juiced Fuel [City]” section yourself, include a short narrative about your city, lifestyle, and why mobile fuel delivery makes sense there. You may leave this blank and our content team will write it for you using best practices for clarity and local SEO.

 Landmark Image

 

 

 

Optional but recommended. Upload a photo of a recognizable local landmark, neighborhood, or lifestyle scene (lake, marina, jobsite, downtown area). This supports visual storytelling on the page.

 Where We Deliver Section

 

 

 

List the cities, towns, neighborhoods, and ZIP codes you plan to serve. Be as detailed as possible. This helps customers quickly understand coverage and improves local search visibility. Bullet-style lists or comma-separated entries are both acceptable.

 Trusted By Section (Optional)

 

 

 

If you already work with local businesses, fleets, marinas, or organizations, list their names here. This section can be expanded later, so it is fine to leave this blank if you are just launching.

 Meet the Owners

 

 

 

Upload a professional headshot for each owner (clear, well-lit, neutral background preferred).
Write a short bio introducing yourself, your background, and your connection to the community. This does not need to be overly polished—our team will refine it for tone, clarity, and consistency across locations.

 Pricing

 

 

 

Enter your current or planned pricing for each service tier. If pricing is still being finalized, you may leave these fields blank and we will display placeholder language similar to the Wichita page until pricing is confirmed.

 Contact the Team Section

 

 

 

Only include public-facing information you want customers to see. This section appears on your live location page.

