Juiced Fuel of Northeast Pennsylvania (NEPA) is a locally owned and operated mobile fuel delivery company dedicated to giving customers back their most valuable resource—time. Serving businesses with small fleets as well as residential customers, Juiced Fuel delivers gasoline and diesel directly to vehicles and equipment, eliminating trips to the pump and reducing downtime. Whether it’s keeping work trucks fueled and ready or making life easier for busy families, Juiced Fuel provides a safe, reliable, and convenient fueling solution designed for today’s on-the-go world.

The franchise is owned and operated by brothers Bill and Chris Kroski, longtime residents of Northeastern Pennsylvania who were born and raised in the region they proudly serve. Their deep local roots and commitment to the community drive the company’s customer-first approach and high standards of service. Together, the brothers combine leadership, teamwork, and real-world experience to build a business grounded in reliability and trust.

Juiced Fuel of NEPA is more than a fuel delivery service—it’s a hometown operation committed to supporting local businesses, simplifying daily routines, and keeping the region moving, one delivery at a time.

 
 

 Save Time

 

 No waiting in line — we bring the fuel to you. 

 
 

 Fuel Anywhere

 

 Driveway, office, school, gym, or marina. 

 
 

 Simple & Secure

 

 Easy in-app payments and emailed receipts. 

 Where We Deliver in NEPA

 

Juiced Fuel is proud to serve drivers, families, businesses, and lake-goers across Northeastern Pennsylvania. Our high-quality fuel delivery service brings fuel directly to you – at home, at work, on the water, or on the job site.

Luzerne & Lackawanna Counties

Lackawanna and Luzerne counties sit at the heart of Northeastern Pennsylvania, where a strong sense of community and a practical, down-to-earth lifestyle define daily life. Rooted in a rich coal-mining and railroad history, the region has evolved into a mix of small cities, tight-knit towns, and rural landscapes where neighbors know one another and local businesses still matter. Residents value reliability, convenience, and services that fit seamlessly into their routines—especially in areas where travel between towns is common and weather can be unpredictable.

Meet Your Local Co-Owners

The franchise is owned and operated by brothers Bill and Chris Kroski, longtime residents of Northeastern Pennsylvania who were born and raised in the region they proudly serve. Their deep local roots and commitment to the community drive the company’s customer-first approach and high standards of service. Together, the brothers combine leadership, teamwork, and real-world experience to build a business grounded in reliability and trust.

Bill Kroski 

Franchise Owner

Bill Kroski is an 18-year veteran of the United States Army, having dedicated his career to service, leadership, and the well-being of others. He currently serves as a physician with the Department of Veterans Affairs, where he provides care to fellow veterans, while also holding the role of Brigade Surgeon in the Army National Guard. His dual commitment to medicine and military leadership reflects a lifelong dedication to those who serve.
Beyond his professional and military career, Bill is driven by an entrepreneurial mindset. He has built a diverse portfolio of real estate investments and is continually seeking opportunities that create value and strengthen local communities. He is particularly excited to enter the fuel delivery and service industry, with a focus on reliably serving his hometown and supporting its growth.
Bill lives in Jenkins with his wife, Kelle, and their three children. Deeply rooted in family, service, and community, he brings discipline, integrity, and vision to every role he undertakes.

Chris Kroski

Franchise Owner

Chris Kroski has built a career defined by teamwork, discipline, and service. He works as a surveyor in heavy civil construction, playing a critical role in complex infrastructure projects that support and strengthen local communities.
In addition to his work in construction, Chris dedicated 14 years to a career in law enforcement, where he served with integrity and a strong sense of duty. His professional background is further shaped by an eight-year career in professional baseball, an experience that reinforced his team-driven mindset, leadership skills, and commitment to excellence.
Chris lives in Duryea with his wife, Jess, and their two daughters. Deeply committed to giving back, he serves his community as the Director of Softball for Grind Athletics and as a Little League coach, helping mentor young athletes and foster teamwork, confidence, and sportsmanship in the next generation.

