--- Juiced Fuel Expands into Central Texas with On-Demand Fuel Delivery ---
URL: https://v1.stageofproject.com/juicedfuel/juiced-fuel-expands-into-central-texas-with-on-demand-fuel-delivery/
Mobile Fuel Delivery Service to Serve Homes, Businesses, Fleets, and Boats Across the Austin Region

Round Rock, TX – Juiced Fuel, the veteran-founded mobile fuel delivery company headquartered in Charleston, South Carolina, is expanding into Central Texas, bringing on- demand fuel delivery to the Greater Austin area and the Highland Lakes.

The Central Texas expansion is led by local owners Clint and Amy Kiemsteadt and Mike and Lisa Hassel, whose decision to launch the business was shaped by firsthand experience with the inefficiencies of traditional fueling.

As lake homeowners and frequent boaters, the families recognized the challenges of fueling boats after time on the water—often requiring either premium marina prices or transporting fuel containers to and from gas stations. At the same time, as parents of daughters living in Austin, they were mindful of the safety concerns associated with late-night gas station stops.

These experiences prompted the families to explore better alternatives, leading them to Juiced Fuel, a mobile fueling platform that delivers fuel directly to homes, businesses, fleet yards, and docks. Recognizing the value of the model, they partnered with Juiced Fuel to bring the service to Central Texas. Using the Juiced Fuel mobile app, customers can schedule fuel delivery where and when it’s needed, receive real-time updates, and eliminate gas station visits altogether.

Juiced Fuel Austin is currently preparing for launch and will begin announcing initial service areas in the coming months. Once live, fuel delivery will be available through the Juiced Fuel mobile app for iOS and Android.

Whether supporting daily commutes, business operations, or time on the water, Juiced Fuel offers a more convenient and reliable way to stay fueled—without detours or delays.

