Chandler, AZ – Juiced Fuel, the app-based mobile fuel delivery service that brings gas directly to customers, is proud to announce its expansion into Arizona’s East Valley, including Chandler and surrounding communities. With this launch, residents and businesses throughout the region will be able to skip the gas station and have fuel delivered directly to their vehicles at home, work, or wherever they are parked.

Juiced Fuel is designed for convenience in a fast-paced world. Using the Juiced Fuel mobile app, customers can request fuel delivery in just a few taps, similar to ordering food through popular delivery apps. The service is ideal for busy professionals, families, and anyone looking to save time by eliminating routine stops at the gas station.

In addition to fueling personal vehicles, Juiced Fuel also provides convenient fueling services for boats, bringing fuel directly to marinas, docks, or storage locations so boat owners can spend more time on the water and less time coordinating fuel stops.

Juiced Fuel also offers white-glove fueling solutions for local businesses and commercial fleets. Companies can schedule recurring fuel deliveries tailored to their operational needs or request fuel on demand through the Juiced Fuel app. This approach helps businesses reduce driver downtime, streamline operations, and improve overall efficiency.

“Juiced Fuel is more than just fuel delivery. It is a service built around people,” said Korey McDavid, CEO of Juiced Fuel. “Our mission is to simplify everyday life by removing the inconvenience of fueling up. The East Valley is a rapidly growing area and a great fit for the convenience that Juiced Fuel provides.”

Leading the East Valley and Chandler expansion are franchise partners Chris and Laura Craig, a dedicated husband-and-wife team focused on bringing modern convenience and dependable service to their local community. Chris and Laura are excited to introduce a new way for residents and businesses to fuel their vehicles without interrupting their busy schedules.

With the East Valley now joining the growing Juiced Fuel network, drivers and boat owners across the region can spend less time at the pump and more time focused on what matters most.

