--- Juiced Fuel Charleston Honors Teachers with Complimentary Gas Fill-Up at St. Andrews School of Math and Science ---
URL: https://v1.stageofproject.com/juicedfuel/juiced-fuel-charleston-teacher-appreciation-st-andrews/
CHARLESTON, S.C. May 8, 2026 In celebration of Teacher Appreciation Week, Charleston-based fuel delivery company Juiced Fuel surprised teachers at St. Andrew’s School of Math and Science today with complimentary fuel fill-ups to their vehicles and special goodie bags as a thank-you for their dedication to students.

Juiced Fuel founders Korey and Caroline McDavid, whose children attend St. Andrew’s School of Math and Science, said the event was a meaningful opportunity to give back to educators who make a lasting impact every day.

“Teachers pour so much into our children, and we wanted to do something tangible to show our appreciation,” said Caroline McDavid. “As parents at St. Andrew’s, we’re grateful for everything the teachers and staff do for our kids and our community.”

Throughout the event, The Juiced Fuel team filled teachers’ tanks with complimentary gas directly on campus while also distributing goodie bags as an added token of appreciation. As part of this special initiative, Juiced Fuel Charleston had the honor of filling up teachers’ vehicles as a small token of appreciation for the big impact they make every single day. In total, we were able to fuel 43 vehicles and provide approximately 254.5 gallons of fuel to deserving members of the St. Andrews Math & Science team.

Juiced Fuel is a mobile fuel delivery service that brings gas directly to customers’ homes, workplaces, fleets, and businesses throughout the Charleston area, helping save time and simplify everyday life.

For more information about Juiced Fuel, visit Juiced Fuel.

For more information about St. Andrew’s School of Math and Science, visit St. Andrews School of Math and Science.

