--- The Silent Bottleneck in Construction Projects: Fuel Access Delays ---
URL: https://v1.stageofproject.com/juicedfuel/silent-bottleneck-construction-projects-fuel-access-delays/
Every construction project plans for delays.

Weather, labor, materials, inspections. Those are expected.

What’s not usually accounted for is something much smaller that quietly impacts all of them: fuel access.

It doesn’t sound like a big deal, but it adds up fast.

A crew shows up ready to work, but a machine is low on fuel. Someone has to leave the site, drive to a gas station, wait, fuel up, and come back. Maybe it’s one truck. Maybe it’s multiple pieces of equipment throughout the day. Either way, that’s time off the job, labor still being paid, and progress slowing down.

And it rarely happens just once.

Fuel interruptions tend to stack. One delay pushes another task back. Equipment sits idle. Schedules tighten. Deadlines start to feel closer than they should.

It’s not dramatic—it’s just constant.

That’s what makes it a silent bottleneck.

On paper, fuel is simple. In reality, it’s one of the most overlooked operational gaps on a job site.

Most crews don’t track it closely because it feels like a routine task. But when you look at it over time, the impact is clear:

Lost labor hours from off-site fueling

Idle equipment waiting to be refueled

Unplanned stops that disrupt workflow

Increased wear caused by inconsistent fueling schedules

None of these issues individually break a project. Together, they slow everything down.

This is where planning around fuel starts to matter.

Instead of reacting when something runs low, more companies are shifting toward scheduled or on-site fueling. Keeping equipment ready before the workday starts removes the need for mid-day interruptions and keeps crews focused on what they’re actually there to do.

It’s not about convenience—it’s about efficiency.

Because in construction, momentum matters. Once it’s broken, it’s hard to get back.

Fuel delivery isn’t new to construction, but the way it’s being used is changing. It’s no longer just for large-scale operations or remote sites. More teams are recognizing that even small inefficiencies, repeated daily, can have a real impact on timelines and costs.

Fuel is one of those things you don’t think about until it slows you down.

And by then, it already has.

--- Why Juiced Fuel Is Changing the Game for Dockside Fueling ---
URL: https://v1.stageofproject.com/juicedfuel/why-juiced-fuel-is-changing-the-game-for-dockside-fueling/
If you’ve ever owned a boat, you already know… fueling it isn’t always the easiest part of the experience.

Getting to a marina can be a process on its own. Depending on where you are, you may be dealing with narrow waterways, no-wake zones, crowded docks, or marinas that aren’t exactly close to where you keep your boat. Some locations are simply harder to access, especially along coastlines, rivers, or tucked-away docks where convenience isn’t part of the setup.

And once you get there, it’s not always quick.

You’re waiting your turn, navigating tight spaces, and paying marina pricing that can feel like a premium just for being there. Add in rising fuel costs, and fueling up starts to feel like a bigger event than it should be.

That’s where Juiced Fuel changes things.

Instead of planning your day around getting fuel, the fuel comes to you. Whether your boat is on a private dock, behind your home, or sitting on a trailer, it gets handled without interrupting your time on the water.

There’s also a major cost advantage that many boat owners don’t initially think about.

Many boats, especially larger ones, require a significant amount of fuel. Two hundred gallons, three hundred gallons, even 500+ gallons isn’t uncommon. At that level, even small price differences per gallon can make a noticeable impact.

With Juiced Fuel, we’re often able to offer fuel options that create meaningful savings compared to ethanol-free marina pricing. In many cases, we’re matching marina prices or beating them outright. When you combine that with not having to burn fuel just to go get fuel, plus the time saved by avoiding the marina altogether, the value starts to add up quickly.

But beyond logistics and pricing, it really comes down to how you want to spend your time.

Boating is supposed to be about being on the water, not waiting at the fuel dock. It’s early mornings, sunset cruises, weekends with family, kids jumping in and out of the water, and friends gathered around. It’s about the experience.

Fueling shouldn’t take away from that.

When your tank is already full before you even untie the boat, everything feels easier. You’re not watching the fuel gauge, planning your route around a fuel stop, or cutting your day short to make sure you can get back to the marina.

You just go.

At the end of the day, Juiced Fuel isn’t just delivering fuel to docks.

It’s removing one of the biggest friction points in boating and turning it into something simple, efficient, and enjoyable.

Because when fueling becomes effortless, you get more of what you bought the boat for in the first place:

Time on the water.

--- Hurricane Season Is Back: Don’t Let Fuel Be the Thing You Forget ---
URL: https://v1.stageofproject.com/juicedfuel/hurricane-season-is-back-dont-let-fuel-be-the-thing-you-forget/
When hurricane season rolls around, most people think about water, batteries, and food. They check flashlights, stock up on supplies, and make a plan. But one thing that consistently gets overlooked until the last minute is fuel.

And by the time people remember, it’s usually too late.

Gas stations get crowded fast. Lines wrap around the block. Stations run out. Traffic gets worse. What should be a quick stop turns into a stressful, time-consuming scramble, all while a storm is getting closer.

Fuel isn’t just another item on the checklist. It’s what keeps everything moving.

Your vehicle, your ability to evacuate, generators, equipment, even small things like helping neighbors or getting to family. When fuel becomes limited, options become limited.

The best way to avoid that stress is simple. Don’t wait.

Topping off early and keeping vehicles consistently fueled throughout the season takes the pressure off completely. Instead of reacting when a storm is announced, you’re already in a position where you can focus on everything else that matters.

This is where having a plan makes a difference.

Keeping your tank above half, knowing where your fuel sources are, and thinking ahead about what you’ll need, not just for your car but for generators or equipment, can save you from making rushed decisions later.

For businesses, especially fleets, the impact is even bigger. Downtime during a storm or right after can be critical. Having fuel ready means being able to respond, recover, and continue operating when others can’t.

Fuel delivery adds another layer of preparation.

Instead of joining the rush, you can schedule fuel ahead of time and keep vehicles and equipment ready without leaving your home or job site. It removes the uncertainty of availability and the risk of waiting in long lines when demand spikes.

In situations like hurricanes, that convenience turns into preparedness.

Hurricane season doesn’t have to feel chaotic.

A little planning goes a long way, and fuel is one of the easiest things to get ahead of if you think about it early. Because when a storm is coming, the last place you want to be is sitting in a gas line, wishing you had taken care of it sooner.

Stay ready, not reactive.

--- Can You Have a Successful Juiced Fuel Franchise Without Being Near Water? ---
URL: https://v1.stageofproject.com/juicedfuel/can-you-have-a-successful-juiced-fuel-franchise-without-being-near-water/
Short answer, yes. And in many cases, you don’t need water at all to build a strong, profitable Juiced Fuel business.

A lot of people immediately associate fuel delivery with boats and marinas, and while that’s a great segment, it’s actually just one piece of the overall market. The majority of demand for fuel delivery happens on land, and it’s consistent, repeatable, and scalable.

The backbone of most successful territories is fleet fueling.

Think HVAC companies, plumbers, electricians, landscapers, construction crews, restoration teams, local service businesses with 5 to 25 vehicles on the road every day. These companies are constantly burning fuel, and every minute their employees spend at a gas station is time they’re not working. Fuel delivery solves a real problem for them by keeping their vehicles ready without interrupting the workday.

That alone can sustain and grow a market.

Then you have everyday consumers.

Busy families, working professionals, parents running kids to school and activities, people who simply don’t want to deal with gas stations anymore. This segment is growing quickly because convenience has become the expectation, not the luxury.

Scheduled weekly or biweekly fueling creates recurring revenue and keeps your routes predictable.

There are also other strong verticals that don’t rely on water at all.

Generators, job sites, equipment, RVs, food trucks, even small recreational vehicles like dirt bikes and ATVs. Anywhere fuel is needed but inconvenient to access becomes an opportunity.

Water can absolutely be a bonus.

If you’re in a coastal or lake-heavy market, boats can add a high-volume, high-margin layer to your business. But it’s not a requirement for success. Some of the most scalable parts of the model are actually land-based because they happen more frequently and are easier to route efficiently.

What really determines success isn’t proximity to water, it’s population density, drive times, and how well you build relationships in your market.

If you’re in an area with enough people, enough vehicles, and enough businesses that rely on fuel daily, the opportunity is there.

At the end of the day, Juiced Fuel isn’t a “boat business.”

It’s a logistics business built around convenience.

And convenience works anywhere people are busy, on the move, and looking for a better way to get things done.

--- How Big Players Are Shaping Marketing (And What Small Businesses Can Do About It) ---
URL: https://v1.stageofproject.com/juicedfuel/how-big-players-are-shaping-marketing-and-what-small-businesses-can-do-about-it/
Marketing today doesn’t feel the same as it used to.

Not because small businesses forgot how to market, but because the game itself has changed. Large companies are spending thousands, sometimes millions, every month to stay in front of customers. They dominate search results, flood social media feeds, and set the baseline for what visibility even looks like.

For a small business, it can feel impossible to compete.

You can have a better product, better service, and stronger relationships, and still get buried simply because someone else is outspending you.

That’s the frustrating part. Visibility is no longer just about quality. It’s often about budget.

But here’s what’s important to understand.

Big companies aren’t just spending more, they’re buying attention at scale. Paid ads, SEO agencies, content teams, constant testing. It creates the illusion that they’re everywhere, all the time.

Small businesses don’t need to match that.

They need to play a different game.

Because what large players gain in reach, they often lose in connection.

They can’t be local in the same way. They can’t build real relationships at the ground level. They can’t show up in communities with the same authenticity or consistency.

That’s where small businesses actually have an advantage, if they lean into it.

Instead of trying to outspend, the shift is toward out-connecting.

That looks like:

Partnering with other local businesses and sharing audiences

Cross-promoting services instead of competing for the same attention

Building referral networks that keep business moving without paid ads

Showing up consistently in your community, both online and offline

These aren’t new ideas, but they’re becoming more valuable as paid marketing gets more saturated.

There’s also a growing shift toward collaboration over competition.

Small business owners are starting to realize that helping each other grow is often more effective than trying to win alone. Sharing customers, supporting launches, and even co-creating content can expand reach without increasing spend.

It builds trust faster too.

Because people don’t just buy from brands anymore. They buy from businesses that feel real, connected, and recommended.

That doesn’t mean marketing doesn’t matter.

It just means it doesn’t always have to be expensive.

Consistency, relationships, and strategic partnerships can go further than a high ad budget when they’re done right.

The reality is, large companies will keep spending.

That’s not changing.

But small businesses don’t need to beat them at their own game to succeed. They just need to stop playing it the same way.

Because attention can be bought.

But trust still has to be earned.

--- Why How Your Employees Present Themselves Matters More Than You Think ---
URL: https://v1.stageofproject.com/juicedfuel/why-employee-presentation-matters-for-your-brand/
Most people think branding lives online. Logos, colors, social media, ads. But in reality, one of the most powerful representations of your business is much simpler than that. It’s your people.

How your employees show up, how they look, how they carry themselves, that’s what customers actually experience in real time. Before a word is even said, there’s already an impression being formed. Is this person identifiable? Do they look like they belong to a legitimate company? Do they seem trustworthy and professional?

Those small details matter more than most business owners realize.

When an employee is clearly branded, whether it’s a uniform, a logo, or even just a consistent look, it removes uncertainty. Customers don’t have to question who is on their property or representing the service. It creates an immediate sense of legitimacy and safety, especially in industries where employees are showing up to homes, job sites, or private locations.

Beyond identification, presentation directly impacts trust. People want to feel confident in who they’re working with. A clean, put-together, professional appearance signals that the business itself is organized and takes pride in what they do. On the flip side, a lack of consistency or effort can create hesitation, even if the service itself is solid.

It also becomes a form of marketing, whether intentional or not.

Every time a truck is parked, a job is being completed, or an employee is interacting in public, they are representing the brand. They are seen by neighbors, other businesses, potential customers. A strong, recognizable presence turns everyday operations into ongoing visibility. It’s subtle, but it builds familiarity over time.

And familiarity builds trust.

The businesses that stand out long term are usually the ones that understand this. They don’t just focus on how they look online, they focus on how they show up everywhere. Because at the end of the day, your employees aren’t just doing the work.

They are the brand people remember.

--- June 17, 2026 Platform Release: Organization Customer Type & Major System Enhancements ---
URL: https://v1.stageofproject.com/juicedfuel/june-17-2026-platform-release-organization-customer-type-major-system-enhancements/
This release significantly expands Juiced Fuel’s business-to-business capabilities with the introduction of the new Organization Customer Type, opening the door to employers, schools, universities, hospitals, community associations, apartment communities, and virtually any organization that serves a group of people who park in the same location. This powerful new customer segment creates opportunities for highly efficient, recurring fuel delivery events that can generate substantially greater delivery density and profitability than traditional consumer deliveries. In addition to these new growth opportunities, this release includes numerous enhancements across scheduling, billing, pricing, reporting, and customer communications designed to improve operational efficiency and provide franchises with greater flexibility and control over their business.

Admin Panel

Organization Customer Type Now Available

The Organization customer type is now fully available and ready for franchise use, opening an exciting new market segment beyond traditional consumer and fleet fueling.
Organizations such as employers, schools, universities, hospitals, apartment communities, homeowner associations, and other membership-based groups can now schedule fuel delivery days at one or more locations, providing a valuable convenience benefit to their employees, students, residents, or members.
Unlike fleet fueling, the organization is not paying for the fuel itself. Instead, the organization sponsors the delivery event, and participating individuals place their own fuel orders for delivery at the designated location and delivery date. Organizations can distribute a unique access code to their constituents, making it easy to coordinate participation and maximize utilization of each fuel delivery event.
Organizations can be managed using either standard subscription plans or custom pricing arrangements, providing franchises with maximum flexibility in how they position and sell the program. For example, smaller organizations may fit well within a standard Organization subscription plan and delivery fee structure, while larger employers, universities, hospitals, or associations may warrant custom pricing based on anticipated participation, delivery frequency, or strategic value. This allows each franchise to tailor its approach to its local market and business development strategy.
This new customer type creates a powerful growth opportunity for franchises by expanding Juiced Fuel into virtually any organization with a group of people who park in the same location. Organizations gain a highly visible employee or member benefit with minimal cost, while franchises gain access to concentrated, recurring delivery opportunities that can generate significantly higher delivery density and profitability than traditional individual consumer deliveries. By serving dozens of vehicles in a single location during a scheduled fuel day, franchises can increase operational efficiency, improve route economics, and unlock an entirely new channel for customer acquisition and recurring revenue growth.
See Video:
1. Juiced Fuel | Admin: Organization Customer Type Now Available – Jun 17, 2026
2. Juiced Fuel | Admin: Organization Participants Orders – Jun 17, 2026

Enhanced Custom Scheduling Visibility
We’ve enhanced custom scheduling to provide better visibility and coordination for
recurring customer deliveries. When a custom schedule is created for a customer and recurring orders are generated from that schedule, all future recurring deliveries will now automatically appear on the customer’s custom scheduling page as well as the territory calendar.
For recurring schedules, the system maintains approximately one month of future visibility by creating the original order plus the next three scheduled orders. As each order is completed, the system automatically generates the next occurrence in the series, ensuring that admins always have a forward looking view of upcoming deliveries without needing to manually create future orders.
This provides a complete view of upcoming deliveries in one place, making it easier to plan resources, coordinate service, avoid scheduling conflicts, and manage fleet or high-touch customer accounts with greater confidence and efficiency. The enhanced visibility also improves forecasting and operational planning by ensuring future scheduled work is always visible on both customer schedules and territory calendars.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Admin: Enhanced Custom Scheduling Visibility – Jun 17, 2026.

Recurring Schedule Deletion Controls
When deleting an order that belongs to a recurring schedule, the system now prompts you to choose whether to delete only that individual order or the selected order and all future orders in the recurring series. This provides greater control and flexibility when managing recurring deliveries, making it easier to modify or discontinue recurring orders when customer needs change.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Admin: Recurring Schedule Deletion Controls – Jun 17, 2026

Expanded Custom Scheduling Flexibility for Closed Days
Custom Scheduling has been enhanced to provide even greater operational flexibility. In addition to allowing deliveries outside normal business hours, admins can now schedule custom deliveries on dates that are marked as closed on the service calendar.
This makes it easier to accommodate special customer requests, fleet fueling needs, after-hours service, emergency deliveries, and other exceptions without being restricted by standard operating schedules. The result is greater flexibility to win and service high-value accounts while maintaining full control over your delivery calendar.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Admin: Expanded Custom Scheduling Flexibility for Closed Days – Jun 17, 2026

Enhanced Payment Status Visibility
Payment Status is now displayed directly on the All Orders, Completed Orders, and Order History grids, allowing admins to quickly identify the payment status of orders without opening each one individually. We’ve also expanded support for payment statuses received from Stripe, including statuses such as Incomplete (commonly used while ACH bank account verification is in progress) and other applicable payment states beyond the previously displayed Unpaid, Pending, and Paid.
This provides faster financial oversight, reduces time spent researching payment issues, and gives franchises a more accurate real-time view of customer payment activity. The enhanced visibility helps your team quickly identify orders requiring attention and better manage collections and customer communications.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Admin: Enhanced Payment Status Visibility – Jun 17, 2026

Universal Invoice & Receipt Access
Admins can now view, send, and manage both Invoices and Receipts for every completed order, regardless of the billing type used. Separate Invoice and Receipt actions are now available directly from the order grids, giving admins the flexibility to manually provide the appropriate document whenever unique customer situations arise.
Automatic emails will continue to be sent based on the standard workflow for each billing type, while admins now have the ability to override that process when exceptions occur.
Real-world billing scenarios don’t always follow the standard workflow.
Whether a COD payment was not collected at delivery, an Invoice Billing customer later requests a receipt after payment, or a credit card payment fails after fuel has already been delivered, admins now have the tools needed to handle these exceptions quickly and professionally. This enhancement improves customer service, reduces administrative workarounds, and provides greater control over billing communications.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Admin: Universal Invoice & Receipt Access – Jun 17, 2026

Manual Payment Status Updates for Invoice Billing
Admins can now manually update Invoice Billing orders as Paid when payment has been received outside of the platform, such as by check, bank transfer, or other offline payment methods. This capability extends the existing functionality available for Cash on Delivery (COD) orders and ensures payment records can accurately reflect real-world collections.
This enhancement eliminates situations where legitimately paid invoices remain indefinitely marked as unpaid within the system. By allowing admins to manually reconcile offline payments, franchises gain more accurate financial reporting, cleaner customer account histories, and improved visibility into outstanding receivables.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Admin: Manual Payment Status Updates for Invoice Billing – Jun 17, 2026

Real-Time Fuel Pricing at Dispatch
To ensure consistent and accurate fuel pricing across all customer types, including Consumer and Fleet customers, fuel prices are now determined at the moment the driver marks the order as “On My Way.” This standardization applies to both standard fuel pricing and custom fleet pricing, ensuring customers are billed based on the most current fuel price available at the time service begins. Additionally, admins can now update fuel prices on orders that have not yet been paid, and drivers retain the ability to adjust fuel prices before submitting the final bill when exceptions are required.
This enhancement eliminates pricing inconsistencies caused by fuel price changes of all types between the time an order is placed and the time it is delivered. Franchises can confidently update fuel pricing as needed, knowing that customers will always receive current pricing at dispatch. The result is more accurate billing, reduced revenue leakage, greater operational consistency, and increased flexibility to handle unique customer situations when necessary.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Admin: Real-Time Fuel Pricing at Dispatch – Jun 17, 2026

Time-Limited Subscription Promotions
Promotions now include a new Subscription Discount Months setting, providing greater flexibility in how subscription discounts are applied. If this field is left blank, the subscription discount will continue indefinitely as a permanent benefit. If a number of months is specified, the discount will automatically expire after the selected number of billing cycles. Previously, subscription promotions could only be configured as either a one-time discount or a permanent recurring discount.
This enhancement gives franchises and corporate marketing teams much more control over promotional campaigns. You can now create compelling offers such as “50% Off for 3 Months,” “$10 Off for 6 Months,” or “Free Delivery for the First 12 Months,” helping drive customer acquisition and retention while automatically transitioning customers to standard pricing at the appropriate time.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Admin: Time-Limited Subscription Promotions – Jun 17, 2026

Failed Payment Notifications
When an order payment or subscription payment fails, the system will now automatically send email notifications to both the customer and the Territory Admin. These notifications provide immediate visibility into payment issues so they can be addressed promptly before they impact future deliveries or subscription renewals.
This enhancement helps reduce missed payments, improves collection efforts, and minimizes the likelihood that payment issues go unnoticed. By proactively notifying both parties, franchises can resolve billing problems more quickly, maintain stronger customer relationships, and reduce revenue leakage caused by failed payment attempts.

Territory-Based Platform Email Reply Routing
All Juiced Fuel platform system notifications are now sent from this centralized platform email address: notifications@juicedfuel.com, to provide a consistent customer experience and strengthen brand recognition. At the same time, replies to those emails are automatically routed to the appropriate franchise support email address based on the customer’s territory using the franchise’s configured Support Email in the platform.
This enhancement delivers the best of both worlds: customers receive professional, branded communications from a single Juiced Fuel email identity, while franchise operators continue to receive and manage customer responses directly. The result is improved brand consistency, simplified email management, and faster customer support by ensuring inquiries are automatically routed to the team best equipped to assist.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Admin: Territory-Based Platform Email Reply Routing – Jun 17, 2026

Enhanced Orders Report
The Orders Report has been significantly expanded with additional data fields to provide a more comprehensive view of order activity across your territories. Previously the report had 13 columns of data and it now has 28 columns of data. The report serves as a centralized source for order information and can be easily exported to Excel for further analysis, reporting, reconciliation, and operational review.
By consolidating more order data into a single report, franchises can spend less time gathering information from multiple screens and more time making informed business decisions. The enhanced reporting supports deeper operational analysis, customer service reviews, financial reconciliation, performance tracking, and custom reporting needs, all while providing the flexibility to work with the data in Excel.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Admin: Enhanced Orders Report – Jun 17, 2026

Customer App (version 1.0.16(Build 5))

Organization Access & Enrollment for Fuel Day Participant
Customers can now add, update, or remove an Organization Access Code at any time through their Profile settings using the new Join Organization option in addition to at initial registration..
When a valid access code is added, the customer is automatically connected to their organization’s fuel delivery program. They can view upcoming organization fuel delivery dates and locations during the ordering process and choose to participate in those deliveries. Customers may also establish recurring orders aligned with their organization’s scheduled fuel delivery days.
Importantly, participation in an organization’s fuel program does not replace the customer’s existing subscription plan. A customer can remain on any consumer plan, such as Boost, VIP, Boats, or other applicable plans, and continue to receive fuel deliveries at their home, marina, or other personal locations. When participating in an organization’s scheduled fuel delivery event, the customer benefits from the organization’s program and is not charged a delivery fee for those deliveries.
This enhancement creates a simpler and faster registration experience for all customers while making organization participation more flexible and accessible. Users can join an organization whenever they are ready, and organizations benefit from an easier enrollment process that encourages greater participation in scheduled fuel delivery events. The result is a smoother customer experience and increased utilization of the Organization customer program.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Customer: Organization Access & Enrollment for Fuel Day Participant – Jun 17, 2026

Self-Service Organization Enrollment
Organizations can now enroll directly through the Customer App and begin offering fuel delivery benefits to their employees, members, students, residents, or other constituents.
During enrollment, organizations can immediately activate service using the platform’s standard pricing structure, allowing them to get started quickly without requiring assistance from Juiced Fuel or the franchise. This will allow for mass marketing to this segment.
For organizations with more specialized needs, franchise administrators retain the ability to customize pricing, delivery fees, subscription options, and service terms. This flexible approach allows smaller organizations to onboard instantly while giving larger organizations access to tailored pricing programs that align with their unique requirements. The result is a faster onboarding experience, greater flexibility, and expanded opportunities for franchises to grow their organizational customer base.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Customer: Self-Service Organization Enrollment – Jun 17, 2026

Driver App (version 1.0.11 (Build 4))

Organization Fuel Day Deliveries
The Driver App now supports Organization fuel delivery events, enabling franchises to efficiently fuel multiple customer vehicles at a single location during a scheduled delivery day. Before the delivery, organization members or employees place their own fuel orders tied to the organization’s scheduled event. The Driver App will display all participating vehicles associated with that delivery, along with the total number of participants, giving drivers visibility into the scope of the fueling event before arriving on site.
During the delivery, drivers will fuel each vehicle individually using a workflow very similar to the existing fleet fueling process, entering gallons and completing service on a vehicle-by-vehicle basis. Once the delivery is completed, the system automatically processes the billing for all participants. Each participating customer is charged for their fuel purchase, while the organization is charged any applicable delivery fees based on its subscription plan or custom pricing arrangement.
This enhancement enables franchises to efficiently service large groups of customers at a single location while maintaining accurate per-vehicle fueling records and automated billing.
By consolidating dozens of individual customer deliveries into a single stop, Organization fuel days can significantly improve route density, increase operational efficiency, reduce delivery costs, and create one of the most scalable and profitable delivery models available within the Juiced Fuel platform.
See Video:
Juiced Fuel | Driver: Organization Fuel Day Deliveries – Jun 17, 2026

--- Next 30 Days Development Roadmap Following the June 17 Release ---
URL: https://v1.stageofproject.com/juicedfuel/next-30-days-development-roadmap-following-the-june-17-release/
1. Multi-Location Fleet Vehicles

Fleet vehicles can now be assigned to multiple approved service locations. This provides greater flexibility for businesses whose vehicles operate from different yards, job sites, offices, or customer locations and simplifies fleet management across multiple locations.

2. Add Vehicles to Existing Fleet Orders

Drivers and administrators will be able to add newly discovered fleet vehicles to an existing order during service. This eliminates the need for separate orders, manual billing adjustments, or workarounds when a customer needs an additional vehicle fueled during a scheduled visit.

3. Admin Controlled ACH Payment Processing

Following a customer’s initial ACH setup, franchise administrators will be able to process future ACH payments directly within the Juiced Fuel Platform. This reduces administrative effort, improves collections, and eliminates the need for customers to repeatedly complete ACH payment requests.

4. Customizable Subscription Plan Messaging

Franchises will gain the ability to customize the subscription plan highlights displayed within the Customer App. Today, most subscription plan descriptions are standardized and limited to ensure consistency and accuracy. This enhancement will allow administrators to manage the key bullet points presented to customers for each subscription plan directly within the Juiced Fuel Platform.

By providing territory-level control over subscription plan messaging, franchises will be able to better communicate the unique benefits of their plans, promote local pricing strategies, highlight special features, and improve customer conversion. Updates can be made without requiring application updates, allowing franchises to quickly adapt their messaging as their offerings evolve.

5. Multiple Fuel Types per Fleet Order

Fleet customers will be able to order multiple fuel types within a single order, with fuel type assigned at the vehicle level. This ensures accurate billing and receipts while reducing manual corrections. Driver workflows will also be enhanced to group vehicles by fuel type, helping prevent fueling mistakes and improving operational efficiency.

6. Multiple Vehicles per Consumer Order

Consumer customers will be able to include multiple vehicles in a single fuel delivery order, provided the vehicles are located at the same address. This creates a more convenient customer experience, reduces duplicate orders, and supports households with multiple vehicles requiring different fuel types.

7. Enhanced Subscription Refund Management

Administrators will gain the ability to refund any subscription payment directly within the Juiced Fuel Platform, regardless of the customer’s current subscription plan. This enhancement provides franchises with the same level of flexibility previously available through Stripe while keeping all payment management activities centralized within the platform.

8. Advanced Subscription Pricing Controls

Franchises will gain significantly more flexibility in how subscription plans are structured and priced. New controls will support vehicle-specific delivery fees, mandatory boat and dock delivery fees, per-gallon surcharges, and per-gallon discounts such as VIP fuel discounts. These improvements will provide greater pricing consistency, eliminate revenue leakage, and give franchises the tools needed to optimize profitability while supporting custom pricing programs and specialized delivery scenarios.

9. Improved Promo Code Experience

The promo code experience within the Customer App will be redesigned to make discounts easier to find, understand, and apply. Improvements will include better promo code placement throughout the ordering and subscription workflows, enhanced visual styling and color consistency, and clearer customer feedback when codes are applied.

In addition, customers will be able to enter valid promo codes in either the subscription or order workflow. If a code is intended for a different purpose (for example, a subscription promotion entered during an order), the platform will provide clear guidance directing the customer to the appropriate location rather than displaying a generic error message. These enhancements will reduce customer confusion, improve promotion redemption rates, and create a more seamless user experience.

10. DEF (Diesel Exhaust Fluid) Support

The Juiced Fuel Platform will support DEF (Diesel Exhaust Fluid) as an optional companion product for diesel fuel deliveries. DEF quantities will be tracked, billed, and reported separately while remaining tied to the associated diesel vehicle. This enhancement creates additional revenue opportunities and better serves commercial diesel fleet customers.

