Item 1
    THE FRANCHISOR AND ANY PARENTS, PREDECESSORS, AND AFFILIATES
       In this disclosure document, “we”, “us,” or “our” refers to Juiced Fuel Franchising LLC
(but not to our officers, director, agents, employees, affiliates, parents or subsidiaries). “You”
means the person to whom we grant a franchise. If you are a corporation, limited liability company,
or other entity, each owner of the franchise entity must sign our Guaranty and Non-Compete
Agreement, which means that all of the franchise agreement’s provisions also will apply to your
owners.

About Us

         Our name is Juiced Fuel Franchising LLC. Our principal business address is 3406 Meeting
Street Rd., North Charleston, SC 29405. We do not have any parent entities. We do not have any
affiliates that offer franchises in any line of business. Our affiliate Juiced Fuel Media LLC provides
marketing services to our franchisees. It has the same business address as us. We do not have any
other affiliates that provide products or services to our franchisees.

         We do not have any predecessors.

       We use the names “Juiced Fuel Franchising LLC” and “Juiced Fuel”. We do not intend to
use any other names to conduct business.

        Our agent for service of process in South Carolina is United States Corporation Agents,
Inc., and the agent’s principal business address is 6650 Rivers Ave., Suite 200, North Charleston,
SC 29406. Our agents for service of process in other states are disclosed in Exhibit A.

         We are a South Carolina limited liability company. We were formed on January 14, 2025.

         We, as the franchisor, do not operate businesses of the type being franchised.

        We do not have any other business activities. We have not offered franchises in other lines
of business.

Information About the Franchises Offered

        If you sign a franchise agreement with us, you will develop and operate a mobile, on-
demand fuel delivery business under the trade name Juiced Fuel. You will have at least two service
trucks, and each truck must have a fuel skid. One truck and fuel skid will serve gasoline customers
and the other with serve diesel fuel customers. Although you will operate a mobile business, you
will need a base of operations where at a minimum you can store vehicles and equipment, and
have fuel tanks on site.

         If you sign a Multi-Territory Addendum, then you will develop and operate multiple
territories, each with at least two trucks and fuel skids. If you have two territories, you must acquire
your third and fourth trucks and fuel skids within one year after commencing business. If you have

                                                   1
Juiced Fuel FDD 2026
Multi-Territory Addendum, then you will develop and operate multiple
territories, each with at least two trucks and fuel skids. If you have two territories, you must acquire
your third and fourth trucks and fuel skids within one year after commencing business. If you have

                                                   1
Juiced Fuel FDD 2026


three or more territories, you must continue to acquire two additional trucks each year until you
have at least two for each territory. Depending on geography, you may be able to use a single base
of operations to support multiple territories.

The general market for fuel delivery services is relatively new and developing. Our
customers are primarily individuals, businesses, and commercial customers that own vehicles,
boats, and/or vehicle fleets. We do not expect there to be any material seasonal variations in the
market unless you service seasonal vehicles (such as boats).

You will compete against traditional fuel outlets, gasoline stations, and established and
emerging fuel delivery services. You will compete against national chains, regional chains, and
independent owners. Some of these competitors are franchised.

Laws and Regulations

In addition to laws and regulations that apply to businesses generally, federal, state and
local jurisdictions have enacted laws, rules, regulations and ordinances which will or may apply
to the operation of your business, including those which (a) regulate matters affecting the health,
safety and welfare of your customers, such as hazardous materials permits, (b) establish standards
pertaining to employee health and safety; (c) establish standards and requirements for spill
remediation and fire safety and general emergency preparedness; and (d) regulate the proper use,
storage and disposal of waste and other hazardous materials. Depending on the location of your
business, you may need to apply for and maintain a motor fuel tax reseller license. You alone are
responsible for investigating and complying with all applicable laws and regulations, despite any
information that we may give you. You should consult with a legal advisor about legal
requirements that may apply to your business, including any permits and licenses necessary to
operate in your market.

Prior Business Experience

We have offered franchises since April 2025.

Our affiliate, Juiced Fuel Inc. has operated Juiced Fuel in Charleston, South Carolina since
December 2022. This affiliate has the same business address as us.

Item 2
                                  BUSINESS EXPERIENCE
Korey McDavid - Chief Executive Officer and Co-Founder. Korey McDavid has been our
