                                               Item 5
                                           INITIAL FEES
Franchise Fee

        When you sign your franchise agreement, you must pay us $49,500 as the initial franchise
fee for a single territory. If you purchase additional territories at the same time, the initial fee for
each additional territory is $40,000. Except for the reduction for multi-territory franchises, this fee
is uniform. This fee is not refundable.

                                                   3
Juiced Fuel FDD 2026
the initial franchise
fee for a single territory. If you purchase additional territories at the same time, the initial fee for
each additional territory is $40,000. Except for the reduction for multi-territory franchises, this fee
is uniform. This fee is not refundable.

                                                   3
Juiced Fuel FDD 2026


In 2025, the initial franchise fee for a single territory ranged from $30,000 (in a multiple-
    territory deal) to $59,500.

Training Fee

When you sign your franchise agreement, you must pay us $5,000 as your initial training
    fee. This fee is uniform and is not refundable.

Technology Onboarding Fee

When you sign your franchise agreement, you must pay us $1,250 for your technology
    onboarding fee, which is used for the initial onboarding for services provided under the
    Technology Fee described in Item 6. This fee is uniform and is not refundable.

Vehicle Wrap Fee

Our vendor for vehicle wraps will wrap your trucks if purchased in Charleston, or they will
    print the wrap and ship it to an authorized installer at your location. The vendor invoices us and
    we invoice you. The cost is currently $3,600 to $3,900 per vehicle, for a total of $7,200 to $7,800
    for two vehicles. You invoice is due and payable within 15 days. It is not refundable.

Go-To-Market Campaign Payment

At least 30 days before you launch your business, you must provide $5,000 to our affiliate
    Juiced Fuel Media LLC for your go-to-market initial marketing campaign. Of this amount, our
    affiliate retains 15% as an agency fee and spends the balance on marketing.

