       If you fail to meet the minimum sales amount in a given territory for any three consecutive
months, we will have the following remedies: we may reduce or take away the territory, or
eliminate your exclusivity in the territory, and/or declare you in default and terminate the franchise
agreement entirely.

         Except as described in this Item, continuation of your territorial exclusivity does not
depend on any contingency and there no other circumstances that permit us to modify your
territorial rights.

Restrictions on Us from Soliciting or Accepting Orders in Your Territory

        Except as described in this paragraph, we will not serve customers in your territory, nor
authorize another party to serve customers in your territory, under our Juiced Fuel brand. However,
we may serve (or authorize other franchisees to serve) customers in your territory if you are in
default, or if you are incapable of meeting customer demand in your territory. We may also serve
(or authorize another franchisee to serve) a particular customer in your territory if you fail to
properly serve such customer, or if we reasonably believe that you will not properly serve such
customer, or if the customer is a national account which you decline to serve. We reserve the right
to use other channels of distribution, such as the internet, catalog sales, telemarketing, or other
direct marketing sales, to make sales within your territory (i) using our principal trademarks, but
only for sales of products or services different from the ones you will offer, and (ii) using
trademarks different from the ones you will use. In the circumstances where the franchise
agreement does not prohibit us from soliciting or accepting orders from inside your territory, we
do not pay any compensation to you.

Soliciting by You Outside Your Territory

        You cannot solicit or market to potential customers outside of your territory, except for
solicitations or marketing which are primarily targeted inside the territory and which incidentally
reach potential customers outside of the territory. You cannot serve customers outside of your
territory without our prior written permission. We may withdraw permission at any time.

Competition by Us Under Different Trademarks

       Neither we nor any of our affiliates operates, franchises, or has plans to operate or franchise
a business under a different trademark selling goods or services similar to those you will offer.
However, the franchise agreement allows us to do so.

